<title>GERMANY: Rains seen aiding German winter crops.</title>
<headline>Rains seen aiding German winter crops.</headline>
<dateline>OFFENBACH 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>German winter crops have received more rain over the past seven days and more is on its way, the DWD meteorological office said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;This will help overcome moisture deficits accumulated during the winter months in the winter grains and rapeseed areas,&quot; a DWD source said.</p>
<p>DWD also forecast milder weather over the next seven days.</p>
<p>Crops should slowly emerge out of dormancy.</p>
<p>There were no further reports of winter damage from eastern Germany after Mecklenburg and Brandenburg states reported some problems earlier in the year.</p>
<p>--Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
